{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>וַיְהִי בְּבֵית אֲדוֹנָיו וגו׳</b> — Behold, Scripture sets forth the rungs of ascent which HaShem raised him. For at first, when they bought him, they assigned him to the labor of slaves who perform outdoor work, since great men do not station slaves to serve in their houses unless the man be worthy and successful. Therefore HaShem ordained success upon him, and through this he came to be in the house of his master, the Egyptian, among the keepers of the house — and this is what it says, <b>וַיְהִי בְּבֵית אֲדוֹנָיו</b>, and not in other labors. He had yet another rank when his master saw, etc., <b>וַיְשָׁרֶת אוֹתוֹ</b> — meaning, he set him apart to serve him exclusively, for through this he would be esteemed and would not live a life of hardship like the lives of lowly slaves. He had yet <b>וַיַּפְקִידֵהוּ עַל בֵּיתוֹ</b> — behold, this gained him authority over all his master's acquisitions. He had yet <b>וַיַּעֲזֹב כָל אֲשֶׁר לוֹ</b> וגו׳. He had yet that he did not know with him, etc. — that he would not know what came in and went out, and he became the sole authority, in Old French mairdomo, over every acquisition of the Egyptian."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "The Old French term מיירדומ׳ (here vocalized מיירדומ״ו) corresponds to Old French mairdomo or major domo, 'head of the household.' I have transcribed it as given and glossed in parentheses."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:06.229360873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}